rules:
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-adr-single-source-of-truth
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture decisions must be recorded and updated only in decision records
    (ADR); all other representations must be derived from ADR.
  title: Rule Adr Single Source Of Truth
- id: rule-aem-consistency-with-decisions
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: AEM must remain consistent with ADR and never contradict decisions.
  title: Rule Aem Consistency With Decisions
- id: rule-architecture-work-authority
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture Work is authoritative source of architectural planning state;
    generated artifacts derive planning status from it.
  title: Rule Architecture Work Authority
- id: rule-core-patterns-must-be-foundational
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Core patterns must represent foundational architectural primitives, not
    specific strategies or implementations.
  title: Rule Core Patterns Must Be Foundational
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-decision-schema-must-be-structured
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All decisions must be expressed using structured YAML decision schema,
    not unstructured narrative.
  title: Rule Decision Schema Must Be Structured
- id: rule-decision-status-drives-stage
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Lifecycle stage derived from decision status; non-accepted items must not
    be DONE.
  title: Rule Decision Status Drives Stage
- id: rule-decisions-must-be-persisted
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All architectural decisions must be persisted as ADR before reflected in
    AEM or other artefacts.
  title: Rule Decisions Must Be Persisted
- id: rule-do-not-merge-across-architectural-layers
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Patterns must not be merged across different architectural layers.
  title: Rule Do Not Merge Across Architectural Layers
- id: rule-generated-artifacts-not-authoritative
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Generated governance artifacts must summarize authoritative sources and
    not become authoritative.
  title: Rule Generated Artifacts Not Authoritative
- id: rule-heuristic-patterns-require-signals
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Heuristic-derived patterns must include at least one linked signal as evidence.
  title: Rule Heuristic Patterns Require Signals
- id: rule-language-semantic-contract
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: 'Defines semantic contract for language: intent vs state, decision vs system
    state, pattern semantics, lifecycle terminology, consistency.'
  title: Rule Language Semantic Contract
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-pattern-decision-lifecycle-alignment
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Pattern maturity and decision lifecycle are distinct but must be interpreted
    consistently.
  title: Rule Pattern Decision Lifecycle Alignment
- id: rule-patterns-born-as-supporting
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All patterns must be created as supporting, never directly core.
  title: Rule Patterns Born As Supporting
- id: rule-precedence-hierarchy
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Global > Project > Prompt rules precedence model for conflict resolution.
  title: Rule Precedence Hierarchy
- id: rule-promotion-requires-evidence
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Pattern promotion to core must be supported by strong evidence from multiple
    sources.
  title: Rule Promotion Requires Evidence
- id: rule-shared-knowledge-workspace
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Projects participate in shared Knowledge Workspace and must not duplicate
    workspace-level governance structures.
  title: Rule Shared Knowledge Workspace
- id: rule-signal-promotion-criteria
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Signal promoted to pattern only when all mandatory criteria satisfied and
    supported by observable evidence.
  title: Rule Signal Promotion Criteria
- id: rule-system-proposes-architect-decides
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All architectural decisions proposed by system and explicitly accepted/rejected/deferred
    by architect.
  title: Rule System Proposes Architect Decides
- id: rule-workflow-execution-model-compliance
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Runtime-native workflows must comply with CAS Workflow Execution Model,
    separation of concerns.
  title: Rule Workflow Execution Model Compliance
summary:
  global_rules: 19
  project_rules: 0
  total_rules: 19
